# Tor SOCKS proxy - applications connect through this
SOCKSPort 9050
# Tor control port - used by tor-control to send commands
ControlPort 9051
# NOTE: no DNSPort. Port 5353 is owned by mDNSResponder on macOS and would fail
# to bind, which makes Tor exit. Apps using the SOCKS proxy send hostnames to Tor,
# so Tor performs the DNS lookups itself.
# Avoid writing to disk for extra privacy
AvoidDiskWrites 1
# Keep tor's data self-contained inside this project folder
DataDirectory ./tor-data